text	principalInvestigatorItemDefText	diva	{"name": "text", "children": [{"name": "recordInfo", "children": [{"name": "validationType", "children": [{"name": "linkedRecordType", "value": "validationType"}, {"name": "linkedRecordId", "value": "divaText"}]}, {"name": "dataDivider", "children": [{"name": "linkedRecordType", "value": "system"}, {"name": "linkedRecordId", "value": "diva"}]}, {"name": "id", "value": "principalInvestigatorItemDefText"}, {"name": "type", "children": [{"name": "linkedRecordType", "value": "recordType"}, {"name": "linkedRecordId", "value": "text"}]}, {"name": "createdBy", "children": [{"name": "linkedRecordType", "value": "user"}, {"name": "linkedRecordId", "value": "161616"}]}, {"name": "tsCreated", "value": "2024-10-30T09:11:22.643014Z"}, {"name": "updated", "children": [{"name": "tsUpdated", "value": "2024-10-30T09:11:22.643014Z"}, {"name": "updatedBy", "children": [{"name": "linkedRecordType", "value": "user"}, {"name": "linkedRecordId", "value": "161616"}]}], "repeatId": "0"}, {"name": "updated", "children": [{"name": "tsUpdated", "value": "2024-11-28T15:43:30.313349Z"}, {"name": "updatedBy", "children": [{"name": "linkedRecordType", "value": "user"}, {"name": "linkedRecordId", "value": "161616"}]}], "repeatId": "1"}, {"name": "updated", "children": [{"name": "tsUpdated", "value": "2024-11-28T15:44:02.782246Z"}, {"name": "updatedBy", "children": [{"name": "linkedRecordType", "value": "user"}, {"name": "linkedRecordId", "value": "161616"}]}], "repeatId": "2"}]}, {"name": "textPart", "children": [{"name": "text", "value": "En projektledare är huvudforskare eller upphovsperson till ett särskilt väldefinierat vetenskapligt projekt (eller annat forskningsprojekt), som en labratorieundersökning eller klinisk prövning. Används ofta som en synonym för ”laboratoriechef\\"."}], "attributes": {"lang": "sv", "type": "default"}}, {"name": "textPart", "children": [{"name": "text", "value": "A principal investigator (PI) is the lead scientist or engineer for a particular well-defined science (or other research) project, such as a laboratory study or clinical trial. It is often used as a synonym for \\"head of the laboratory,\\" not just for a particular study. In the context of USA federal funding from agencies such as the NIH or the NSF, the PI is the person who takes direct responsibility for completion of a funded project, directing the research and reporting directly to the funding agency.[1] For small projects (which might involve 1-5 people) the PI is typically the person who conceived of the investigation, but for larger projects the PI may be selected by a team to obtain the best strategic advantage for the project. In the context of a clinical trial a PI may be an academic working with grants from NIH or other funding agencies, or may be effectively a contractor for a pharmaceutical company working on testing the safety and efficacy of new medicines. "}], "attributes": {"lang": "en", "type": "alternative"}}]}
