text	ssifCollectionDefText	diva	{"name": "text", "children": [{"name": "recordInfo", "children": [{"name": "validationType", "children": [{"name": "linkedRecordType", "value": "validationType"}, {"name": "linkedRecordId", "value": "divaText"}]}, {"name": "dataDivider", "children": [{"name": "linkedRecordType", "value": "system"}, {"name": "linkedRecordId", "value": "diva"}]}, {"name": "id", "value": "ssifCollectionDefText"}, {"name": "type", "children": [{"name": "linkedRecordType", "value": "recordType"}, {"name": "linkedRecordId", "value": "text"}]}, {"name": "createdBy", "children": [{"name": "linkedRecordType", "value": "user"}, {"name": "linkedRecordId", "value": "161616"}]}, {"name": "tsCreated", "value": "2024-10-04T12:57:27.147365Z"}, {"name": "updated", "children": [{"name": "tsUpdated", "value": "2024-10-04T12:57:27.147365Z"}, {"name": "updatedBy", "children": [{"name": "linkedRecordType", "value": "user"}, {"name": "linkedRecordId", "value": "161616"}]}], "repeatId": "0"}, {"name": "updated", "children": [{"name": "tsUpdated", "value": "2024-10-04T13:52:41.584841Z"}, {"name": "updatedBy", "children": [{"name": "linkedRecordType", "value": "user"}, {"name": "linkedRecordId", "value": "161616"}]}], "repeatId": "1"}]}, {"name": "textPart", "children": [{"name": "text", "value": "Standard för svensk indelning av forskningsämnen är en statistisk standard för klassificering av forskning och utbildning på forskarnivå. Standarden används även i viss utsträckning vid ansökan om forskningsmedel och vid klassificering av forskningsoutput. Tillhandahållen av Statistiska centralbyrån (SCB) och Universitetskanslersämbetet (UKÄ).\\n "}], "attributes": {"lang": "sv", "type": "default"}}, {"name": "textPart", "children": [{"name": "text", "value": "Standard for Swedish classification of research subjects is a statistical standard for classification of research and education at postgraduate level. The standard is also used to a certain extent when applying for research funding and when classifying research output. Supplied by Statistics Sweden (SCB) and Swedish Higher Education Authority (UKÄ)"}], "attributes": {"lang": "en", "type": "alternative"}}]}
